      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "Our fleet modernization continues!\n\nThe Coast Guard recently accepted delivery of our 19th C-130J Super Hercules aircraft (CGNR 2019). With greater speed, range and endurance, this aircraft drastically expands our operational reach and maritime domain awareness.\n\nThe aircraft’s improved capabilities will help our crews save lives, respond to contingencies, and secure U.S. borders and maritime approaches, while supporting a wide range of critical operations.\n\nFollowing missionization, CGNR 2019 is expected to enter operational service in 2027.\n\nRead the full press release here: https://t.co/Ww74buHZU0\n@DHSgov",
      "text_resolved": "Our fleet modernization continues!\n\nThe Coast Guard recently accepted delivery of our 19th C-130J Super Hercules aircraft (CGNR 2019). With greater speed, range and endurance, this aircraft drastically expands our operational reach and maritime domain awareness.\n\nThe aircraft’s improved capabilities will help our crews save lives, respond to contingencies, and secure U.S. borders and maritime approaches, while supporting a wide range of critical operations.\n\nFollowing missionization, CGNR 2019 is expected to enter operational service in 2027.\n\nRead the full press release here: https://www.news.uscg.mil/Press-Releases/Article/4509942/coast-guard-takes-delivery-of-19th-hc-130j-long-range-surveillance-aircraft/\n@DHSgov",
